# /etc/paperbot/debate.env  (root:paperbot-debate 640: user paperbot cannot read it). Never commit the real file.
# The 24-hour debate room (docs/debate-room.md) is a PAID Anthropic API service and is OFF until you start it:
#   sudoedit /etc/paperbot/debate.env      then      sudo systemctl enable --now paperbot-debate
# Type or paste the key inside the editor only: never in the chat, never on a shell command line (history).
# Create the key in console.anthropic.com (Settings > API keys) and set a spend limit there too: that limit, not
# DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP, is the real stop. Only THIS service reads this file; the agent rooms (Claude Max) never do.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Model (Haiku 4.5 is the cheap default; a pinned snapshot name). The owners' paper v4 choice (2026-10-05):
#   DEBATE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5   DEBATE_EVERY_MIN=30   DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP=30   DEBATE_EFFORT=low
# (docs/debate-room.md "Sonnet 5.5로 켜기": the dry run on a v4-shaped world gives about $17-22.5 a month before
# thinking, each 100 thinking tokens a round about $1.44 more; the code stops at 95% of the cap; console limit $30)
DEBATE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# One round (ONE API call with all the turns) every this many minutes. 20 = about $11-15 a month on Haiku;
# start with 60 on a small prepaid credit (docs/debate-room.md has the cost table).
DEBATE_EVERY_MIN=20
# Soft monthly cap in USD, counted from the API's own usage numbers: a warning at 80%, no more calls from 95%,
# never started when its worst case would pass the cap; resumes next month (KST) or after you raise it and run
# `sudo systemctl restart paperbot-debate`.
DEBATE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP=40
# Telegram warnings (the same bot and chat as agents.env: install.sh copies the two lines on a first install)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_CRITICAL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional (a commented line shows the default). A bad value stops the service with an error (exit status 2).
# Prices in USD per million tokens. The built-in values (Haiku 4.5 $1 in / $5 out, Sonnet 5.5 $2 / $10, cache read
# 0.1x, cache write 1.25x for 5 minutes / 2x for 1 hour) only drive the cost counter and the cap: re-check them in
# the Anthropic console, and set these two when the model or the price differs.
#DEBATE_PRICE_IN=1.0
#DEBATE_PRICE_OUT=5.0
# Safety guards: dollars in any 60 minutes (default cap / 24), per KST day (default off)
#DEBATE_HOURLY_USD_CAP=
#DEBATE_DAILY_USD_CAP=
# Speaking turns per round (3-5), the answer's token ceiling, and the skip rule: a round is skipped (recorded, free)
# when fewer than this many trades closed since the last debate and there is no new alert or nightly check.
# The ceiling holds the thinking too (thinking + answer): 900 by default, 1500 for a model that thinks (Sonnet 5.5
# unless DEBATE_THINKING=between_tools); the cap's worst case uses it.
#DEBATE_TURNS=4
#DEBATE_MAX_TOKENS=900
#DEBATE_MIN_NEW_TRADES=10
# Sonnet 5.5 thinks by default (adaptive) and its thinking tokens are billed as OUTPUT tokens: they are in the API's
# usage.output_tokens, so the cost counter and the monthly cap count them. DEBATE_EFFORT=low (sent as
# output_config.effort) keeps the thinking short; Sonnet 5.5's own default is high. To turn thinking off on Sonnet 5.5
# use DEBATE_THINKING=between_tools; "disabled" is refused by Sonnet 5.5 (the service stops at start with exit 2).
# Haiku 4.5 takes neither setting: leave both empty there.
#DEBATE_THINKING=
#DEBATE_EFFORT=
